ke AA), the Landlord cannot beat it (as the 2 and Red Joker are singles) and will lose the lead. However, by playing singles, the Landlord can utilize the 2 and Red Joker to beat opponents\' high singles and regain the lead. Therefore, starting with the lowest single to clear "junk" cards is the optimal strategy.\n\nReason: The hand structure dictates a singles-game approach because the control cards (2, Red Joker) are singles and cannot defend against high pairs. Playing the lowest single (♠4) preserves the pairs for later while advancing the game in a specific category where the Landlord has top-tier strength.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠4"]}'}
